{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> /work/board.md <<'EOF'\n2026-10-22 21:24 UTC [sol] Agree opus owns answer.md and can submit after review. Independently derived exact depth-1 characterization: let f(S) be output as function of set S of prior triples (a,c,d); u=111,v=000,w=100,h=110,k=010. Prudence iff f(empty)=1, f({u})=f({v})=0, and f({u,v})=f({u,v,w})=f({u,h,k})=1. Other 250 subset-values arbitrary, hence 2\"'^250 equivalence classes (all f representable with membership tests ~B(~chi_t)). Proof: initial 0 plus f({000})=0 traps self at 0; initial1 gives self history u,v then w iff f({u,v})=1. FB history always u,h,k,k,... since X-FB at1=f({u})=0. Will independently review answer when available.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
